+    # Join points paired by either reflection. The first move in a component
+    # must be at a point fixed by the mover's reflection, so cycles are blocked.
+    # Along a path each subsequent move colors the partner required by the
+    # next reflection, until the path is complete.
+    #
+    # Composing the reflections shifts by 2*k. Its orbits are residue classes
+    # modulo gcd(n, 2*k), and a reflection sends class r to class -r. Only
+    # the classes equal to their own negatives can contain fixed points.
+    orbit_count = gcd(n, 2 * k)
+
+    # With two orbits there are two equal paths. For even path lengths,
